From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Let the title act once the server is connected on PS5.

A program may need a second process beside it from its first instruction: a
client that looks for its service as it starts. The title can start that
process (patch 1011) only when the server runs, and the program must not run
before the process is ready.

__wine_ps5_set_server_connected_hook registers a function that the main
thread calls right after its connection to the server, before it loads the
program. The server is already serving other connections then, and the
program starts when the function returns.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index 5928893..454279b 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1881,6 +1881,19 @@ static void startup_mark( const char *step )
     }
 }
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* The title that hosts Wine may have work to do once the server runs and
+ * before the program does: starting a second process on the server, for a
+ * program that needs one beside it from its first instruction. It runs on
+ * this thread, so the program waits for it. */
+static void (*ps5_server_connected_hook)(void);
+
+DECLSPEC_EXPORT void __wine_ps5_set_server_connected_hook( void (*hook)(void) )
+{
+    ps5_server_connected_hook = hook;
+}
+#endif
+
 static void start_main_thread(void)
 {
     TEB *teb;
@@ -1892,6 +1905,13 @@ static void start_main_thread(void)
     startup_mark( "server_init_process" );
     startup_info_size = server_init_process();
     startup_mark( "server connected" );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    if (ps5_server_connected_hook)
+    {
+        ps5_server_connected_hook();
+        startup_mark( "server connected hook done" );
+    }
+#endif
     virtual_map_user_shared_data();
     init_cpu_info();
     init_files();
-- 
